---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout canonicalPath="/about">
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-50 bg-gradient-to-b from-navy to-navy-deep shadow-lg border-b border-white/10">
    <nav class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <img src="/icon-white.svg" alt="CharterWise" class="h-9 w-9" />
        <span class="text-white font-bold text-2xl tracking-tight">CharterWise</span>
      </a>
      <a
        href="/"
        class="text-white/80 hover:text-white transition-colors text-sm font-medium"
      >
        Back to home
      </a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="bg-white min-h-screen flex items-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mb-12">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#D4A843] mb-4">About</p>
        <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold text-[#1B3A5C] mb-8">
          Built by a sailor who wanted better intel.
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-[#6B7280] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          I'm Clément, a 40-year-old based in London with a background in technology and operations. Over the past decade, I've worked at Google and Meta in Operations and Customer Support — roles that taught me how to listen to users, spot systemic problems, and build solutions that actually work.
        </p>

        <p>
          Outside of work, I'm a sailor. I've chartered boats regularly across the Mediterranean, Caribbean, and beyond with friends and family. And each time, I noticed the same thing: arriving at the marina without clear visibility into what's actually working on the boat — the water maker, navigation systems, galley equipment, safety gear. Charter listings show marketing photos, but sailors need practical intel about condition and maintenance.
        </p>

        <p>
          The more charters I did, the more I realised the gap wasn't really about listings — it was about how little the charter company itself could see. A boat comes back at 10am, another guest is due at 5pm, and the handover in between often runs on a paper clipboard: no photos worth keeping, no timestamp, no record beyond a signature. If a fender's missing or the watermaker's dead, it's a phone call and a guess.
        </p>

        <p class="font-semibold text-[#1B3A5C]">
          CharterWise Fleet exists because those two parts of my life — technology and sailing — finally intersected. I built the digital handover that charter companies were missing: verified condition data captured at every pickup and return, so a fleet manager always has an accurate, current read on every boat — and the next charterer steps onto something better than the last guest left it.
        </p>

        <p>
          It's built on a simple principle: the people actually standing on the boat — guests, skippers, base managers — know its real condition best. Capturing that moment digitally, instead of re-compiling it from memory afterward, is what makes the record trustworthy.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you run a charter fleet and want a clearer, more accurate read on where things actually stand, I'd love to hear from you. This is still early, and I'm building it with the operators who use it.
        </p>

        <div class="pt-6 border-t border-[#E5E7EB]">
          <p class="text-sm">
            <span class="font-semibold text-[#1B3A5C]">Get in touch:</span><br />
            <a href="mailto:hello@charterwise.app" class="text-[#D4A843] hover:text-[#E5B95A] transition-colors">hello@charterwise.app</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="bg-[#1B3A5C] text-white/60 py-10">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <img src="/icon-white.svg" alt="CharterWise" class="h-6 w-6 opacity-80" />
        <span>
          <span class="font-bold text-white">CharterWise</span>
          <span class="ml-2">— Fleet operations intelligence for charter companies.</span>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
        <a href="/about" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">About</a>
        <a href="/privacy" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Privacy</a>
        <a href="mailto:hello@charterwise.app" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 mt-6 text-xs text-white/30 text-center sm:text-left">
      © {new Date().getFullYear()} CharterWise Ltd. Built by a sailor, for the people running the fleet.
    </p>
  </footer>
</Layout>
